From aaa0c2b2a2e38a6dd66cba2f5e2e47a1ac8f11fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:56:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MPEG: feed the IPU bitstream a game sends over the toIPU DMA

CRI Sofdec (Soulcalibur III's movies) keeps its video bitstream in a ring of 2 KiB sectors and points the toIPU DMA (channel 4) at it, one REF tag per sector; libmpeg asks for more through the game's Nodata callback.

- PS2Memory hands normal and source-chain toIPU transfers to an IPU input sink, updates MADR/TADR/QWC/CHCR.TAG and raises CIS4. A full decoder stalls a chain at a tag boundary. Before a restart the sink is asked whether it can take input: taking another sector with eight pictures queued ran past Sofdec's REFE, made its readable block count negative and replayed stale data.
- sceMpegCreate installs the sink, which feeds that decoder unless the stub demuxes the stream itself (sceMpegAddBs, PSS).
- sceMpegGetPicture calls the Nodata callback when no picture is ready, as libmpeg does, and retries, after a VBlank when nothing came of it. The flag the game sets in mp->sys+0x878 when its input is used up ends the stream, and the end is published in sys word 0 for the game's own sceMpegIsEnd.
- sceMpegAddCallback replaces an earlier callback of the same type (libmpeg has one per type), so a decoder recreated over the same handle does not keep the previous movie's registration. Stream callbacks are unchanged.

Tests: toIPU chain, normal, remainder and stall/restart transfers (a restart while full takes nothing); Nodata is called with its registered data, a re-registration replaces the old one, the end flag ends GetPicture and reaches sceMpegIsEnd; with FFmpeg, a 32x32 MPEG-2 stream sent over the DMA decodes.
